<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A section that expands and collapses to show or hide its content.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/collapsible)

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Collapsible do
  CollapsibleTrigger { "What's included in the free plan?" }
  CollapsibleContent { "Up to three projects, 1 GB of storage, and community support." }
end
```

Collapsible is a single show/hide disclosure - one trigger controlling one panel. Reach for it for a
"read more", an inline details section, or any one-off toggle. Compose it from three parts:

- **Collapsible** - the root. Owns the open state (`open:`) and can be `disabled:`.
- **CollapsibleTrigger** - the button that toggles the panel. It exposes `data-panel-open` and
  `data-disabled` for styling.
- **CollapsibleContent** - the panel, which animates its height open and closed through the
  `--collapsible-panel-height` CSS variable.

The parts ship almost unstyled so the collapsible inherits your layout - the examples add the chevron and
spacing. The state is rendered on the server (`data-open` / `data-closed` on the root), so the page is
right before JavaScript loads; the `appica-ui--collapsible` controller toggles and animates it.

## Examples

### File tree

Nest a Collapsible inside another Collapsible's content to build an expandable tree. Each folder is its
own disclosure; files are plain rows.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :file_tree %>

```ruby
def tree_item(node)
  return span { node.name } unless node.children?

  Collapsible do
    CollapsibleTrigger(class: "group inline-flex items-center gap-1.5") do
      chevron(class: "group-data-panel-open:rotate-90")
      plain node.name
    end
    CollapsibleContent { div(class: "ms-2 border-s ps-2") { node.children.each { |child| tree_item(child) } } }
  end
end
```

### Settings panel

Reveal extra controls only when they're needed. The trigger renders as a Button through its block argument,
and the icon swaps from the root's `data-open` state (`group-data-open:`) - no extra JavaScript.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :settings_panel %>

```ruby
Collapsible(class: "group") do
  CollapsibleTrigger do |trigger|
    Button(**trigger, variant: :outline, size: :sm, icon: true, aria_label: "Set each corner individually") do
      maximize_icon(class: "group-data-open:hidden")
      minimize_icon(class: "hidden group-data-open:block")
    end
  end
  CollapsibleContent { ... }
end
```

### Show more

Because the trigger and panel are independent, the trigger can sit below the always-visible text, with its
label following the open state.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :show_more %>

### Controlled

Any button inside the root drives it with `data: { action: "appica-ui--collapsible#toggle" }` (or `#open` /
`#close`). The controller dispatches `appica-ui--collapsible:open-change` with `{ open }`.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :controlled %>

### Disabled

`disabled: true` locks the panel shut. The trigger drops out of the tab order and exposes `data-disabled`.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :disabled %>

### Hidden until found

Closed panels carry the `hidden` attribute. With `hidden_until_found: true` they use the native
`hidden="until-found"` instead, so the browser's find-in-page (and crawlers) can reach the text - and a
match opens the panel.

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :hidden_until_found %>

### RTL

The trigger and panel align to the right, the indent moves via the logical `ps-*` padding, and the chevron
mirrors (`rtl:-scale-x-100`).

<%= embed AppicaUI::CollapsiblePreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Collapsible

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `open:` / `default_open:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Initial open state. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Disable the trigger so the panel can't toggle. |
| `id:`, `class:`, `data:`, … | | | Other attributes go on the root `<div>`. |

The root carries `data-open` / `data-closed`; the controller exposes the `toggle`, `open` and `close`
actions and the `appica-ui--collapsible:open-change` event.

### CollapsibleTrigger

Renders a `<button>` with `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls`, `data-panel-open` and `data-disabled`. A block
taking an argument receives these attributes to put on your own element (e.g. a `Button`).

### CollapsibleContent

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `hidden_until_found:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Use `hidden="until-found"` so closed text stays findable. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Renders a `<div>` with `data-open` / `data-closed`.

## Accessibility

- `CollapsibleTrigger` is a real `<button>` with `aria-expanded` reflecting the state and `aria-controls`
  pointing at the panel, so assistive tech announces "expanded" / "collapsed".
- Enter and Space toggle the panel while the trigger is focused.
- A disabled collapsible removes the trigger from the tab order and marks it `data-disabled`.
- Indicator icons (the chevrons in these examples) are decorative - the trigger's text carries the meaning.
- The height animation honors `prefers-reduced-motion`, collapsing instantly.
